  "asked": "# Build: kill-patches-pilot (Urgent profile) Requested by Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice): \"Patches is dead. Delete it, all references. Build Pilot dead, same thing. Delete it. All references.\" GO given. Do it now. ## First - Register in the Urgent profile via the orchestrator CLI (id `kill-patches-pilot`, branch claude/kill-patches-pilot) + banner entry. Never hand-edit store.json (orch-live-sync is running). Other parallel builds: notes-vault, headless-tabs, whats-new-banner, amberx-backup-fix. ## Remove from this repo (AmberX-AXF), everything - Patches: apps/patches-web, the Patches Android app/module, any patches plugin/wrapper code, patches-specific assets, banners, boilerplates, catalog/tracker entries, CI workflow jobs and deploy steps, rebake targets, demo/walkthrough chapters or captions mentioning it, help packs, docs (_claude/memory/docs/patches-*, rebuilds/patches-*), tracker.json rows. - Build Pilot: any build-pilot app/plugin/tab/integration code, Dev Console or axHub hooks into it, catalog/docs/help/walkthrough references. - Rules/instructions: rewrite every rule that depends on Patches. In particular the hub-sync rule that \"Console and Pilot can only run inside Patches (never standalone)\" -> Console runs standalone; Pilot is gone. Update RULES.md (repo + shared), CLAUDE.md, THREADS.md (one closing line, don't rewrite history), STATUS, decisions.md (add a decision entry: Patches and Build Pilot retired Nov 3 2026; don't delete old decision text, mark superseded). - Orchestrator store: archive every build whose subject is Patches or Build Pilot (via CLI), note \"retired Nov 3 2026\". Pending queue too. - grep -ri 'patches\\|build.pilot\\|build-pilot\\|buildpilot' across the repo afterward; the only hits left may be historical log lines and the decision entry. Note: don't confuse with generic words like 'patch' / 'patching' / 'autopilot' / PilotX (separate app). - Everything must still build: tsc, vite builds of every remaining app, check-theme/check-controls, plugin lifecycle, CI block. Open the PR. ## Remove from the VPS (live) - Before removing anything: snapshot each container's volumes/data + its Coolify app config to /root/archive/retired-2026-11-03/ (tar.gz), so it's recoverable. - Stop and remove the `patches-web` and `build-pilot` containers and their Coolify applications (Coolify API/UI so they don't come back on redeploy), Traefik routes/domains, any cron/systemd units, images. - axHub projects tree: remove /projects/patches, /projects/patches-web (and any build-pilot project) via the hub memory API so versions stay recoverable; remove them from shared/memory/projects.md. - axHub repo: references to Patches/Build Pilot (services, examples, docs, approvals) -> clone /root/axHub fresh on branch claude/kill-patches-pilot, remove them, open a PR there too. - GitHub repo MossesX/Build-Pilot: ARCHIVE it (read-only), do not delete; deleting a repo is irreversible and Brett can delete it in one click later. Say so in the report. ## Report `_claude/builds/reports/kill-patches-pilot.md`: everything removed (paths, containers, apps, domains), where the archive is, PR links. Mark each step done through the store as you go. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
